<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Paardeberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Paardeberg was fought from 18 to 27 February 1900 on the Modder River, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-roberts-1st-earl-roberts">Lord Roberts</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herbert-kitchener">Lord Kitchener</a> surrounded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piet-cronje">Piet Cronjé</a>'s retreating army and, after a costly assault and a siege of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> laager, forced about 4,000 men to surrender. The defeat opened the way for the British capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bloemfontein">Bloemfontein</a> in March 1900.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-paardeberg.jpg" alt="Battle of Paardeberg" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Canadian_Infantry_at_Paardeberg,_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
